{"title":"Security Engineer Roadmap","role":"Security Engineer","summary":"A Security Engineer designs, implements, tests, monitors, and improves systems that protect applications, networks, endpoints, cloud infrastructure, IoT devices, and data from cyber threats.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"CSE – Cyber Security & IoT incl. Blockchain"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Security Engineer designs, implements, tests, monitors, and improves systems that protect applications, networks, endpoints, cloud infrastructure, IoT devices, and data from cyber threats."},{"type":"flow","items":["For a Cyber Security","IoT","Blockchain graduate, the strongest profile combines:"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Computer networks"},{"text":"Linux"},{"text":"Operating systems"},{"text":"Programming"},{"text":"Cloud security"},{"text":"Application security"},{"text":"IoT security"},{"text":"Identity and access management"},{"text":"Security monitoring"},{"text":"Digital forensics"},{"text":"Blockchain security"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The career should be positioned primarily around cybersecurity engineering, with IoT and blockchain as specialist domains rather than treating all three as equal career tracks."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Security Engineer can eventually specialize in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cybersecurity Engineering"},{"text":"Network Security"},{"text":"Cloud Security"},{"text":"Application Security"},{"text":"Product Security"},{"text":"DevSecOps"},{"text":"SOC Engineering"},{"text":"Detection Engineering"},{"text":"Identity & Access Management"},{"text":"IoT/OT Security"},{"text":"Mobile Security"},{"text":"Security Automation"},{"text":"Digital Forensics"},{"text":"Threat Detection & Response"},{"text":"Blockchain/Web3 Security"},{"text":"Security Arc